  "answer": "The study did not reach its goal. The code counts 3 of the 5 settings as confirmed, and only 2 of those show the policy failing. On 096988dd (cars 2 s later at 1.25x speed) and 09a95ffa (recorded timing at 1.25x speed), every run failed the same way: the policy made a lane change to the left that the route did not ask for, and hit a car driving alongside in that lane. The third setting, 023b7fcc at 2 s earlier and 1.5x, does clear the bar, but in every run there a retimed car hit the ego from behind before the policy took control. The plan said to ignore rear-end hits, so this setting shows a replay problem, not a policy failure. Each confirmed setting rests on only a few runs, so its range only shows the failure rate is above one half. The failures look tied to faster cars in the adjacent lane, not to cars cutting in, and this setup cannot tell those two apart.",
